INT. STALLED ELEVATOR, TWENTY-SECOND FLOOR - DAY

A mahogany-panelled elevator with a brass nameplate: CALLOWAY & PRIDE, ASSET MANAGEMENT. The numbers above the door read 22 and flicker. On the floor sits a large sheet cake in a cardboard box.

HORACE PRIDE, sixty, the firm's senior partner, in a three-piece suit, grips the handrail. GLORIA MENDELSOHN, forty, an executive assistant with an orange lanyard, holds a clipboard to her chest. TERRENCE "TERRY" BOOTH, twenty-five, a mailroom clerk, clutches a bundle of envelopes and a balloon on a string.

The elevator lurches. Horace and Gloria both grab for the cake box. Terry throws himself across it. The three of them end up in a heap on the carpet, the balloon bobbing above them, the cake intact.

HORACE
Get off the cake!

TERRY
I'm saving the cake!

GLORIA
You're sitting on the cake!

Terry rolls away. Gloria lifts the lid. Across the top, in blue icing: CONGRATULATIONS ON YOUR RETIREMENT, HORACE.

HORACE
I'm not retiring.

GLORIA
That's what the memo said.

HORACE
What memo?

GLORIA
The one signed by you.

HORACE
I sign forty memos a day.

TERRY
Sir, the party's at three.

HORACE
What party?

GLORIA
Yours.

HORACE
I never agreed to a party.

GLORIA
You agreed to the memo.

HORACE
I agreed to a memo about a party. Not a party about my retirement.

TERRY
Is there a difference?

HORACE
There is a difference, Terrence. The difference is that I'm not ready.

GLORIA
You're sixty-three, Horace. Everybody else on the floor has been ready for you since 2014.

HORACE
That is a cruel thing to say to a man in an elevator.

GLORIA
It is a true thing. The cruelty is incidental.

TERRY
Should I, uh. Should I press the button again?

HORACE
Press whichever one gets me out of this conversation.

Terry presses every button on the panel at once. The elevator groans, lurches, and drops a floor. Horace and Gloria clutch the rail. Terry hugs the cake. The balloon floats up and pops against the ceiling.

The doors slide open on the sixteenth floor. A crowd of colleagues in party hats stares in, holding streamers.

COLLEAGUES (O.S.)
Surprise!

Horace and Gloria look at each other. Terry, still on the floor, lifts the cake, a little squashed, a lot proud.

HORACE
I am going to need a very large drink.
